cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DriveBench, cite this software and record the exact Git commit and benchmark protocol used."
type: software
title: "DriveBench: Verifiable Rewards for Lossy World-Model Inference"
authors:
  - family-names: Mahadik
    given-names: Rahul
repository-code: "https://github.com/rahul-mahadik/driving-world-model-inference"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software toward verifiable rewards for lossy inference optimization
  of video world models. Modern baselines, calibrated quality verification,
  tabulated configuration search, and hardware transfer are staged research
  goals. Historical measurements remain separate from unrun studies. This
  software citation does not identify a peer-reviewed paper or completed
  validation of a general-purpose code-action benchmark.
